    "passage": "Commonly known as a painkiller, aspirin can also work wonders for people worried about their heart health, or so many experts thought. Aspirin, when [[1]] in low doses on a daily basis, is believed to be an amazing blood thinner that can bring down chances of heart disease and stroke. Given such [[2]], aspirin has enjoyed decades of popularity with the public and the medical community. However, recent research has linked the powerful blood-thinner to higher risks of bleeding inside human body. The possible harms of daily dosage of aspirin will probably outweigh the benefits [[3]].\nNow, decades after issuing the medical guideline suggesting aspirin for improving heart health, the health authorities in the US finally modified the age-old recommendation, and started instead to [[4]] the idea of taking aspirin for the sole purpose of staying away from heart disease or stroke. Those who are currently on aspirin for other health issues, [[5]], will still do well to stay on the medication unless their doctors suggest differently. They had better consult their doctors before making any changes.",
